Zero Conditional Sentences: Grammar rule for if-clauses referring to general truths (If + present, present)'),
  ('b7c681c577eca76cd1868dd2bcc56c80', 'entrance', 'Biology', 'Biology(Grade-12) Exit Exam Comprehensive Revision Note', 'Antibody: A blood protein produced in response to and counteracting a specific antigen
